I'm learning dplyr. I have spent some time reviewing the Databases vignette. The only place it mentions creating an index on a database is using the copy_to function when initially creating the database. What if I have an existing sqllite database and I want to add an index to it? My understanding is that copy_to is meant to copy some local memory data frame into a database. I'm not sure it's really needed if I already have the database. Am I wrong or is there some other approach?

