Hi:

The rowwise() function can replace group_by() in this problem. The
following works for me:

library(dplyr)

df <- data.frame(x=c("a", "b", "c"), start=1:3, end=4:6, val=c(100, 200, 300))

df %>%
   rowwise() %>%
   do(with(., data.frame(x = x, n = seq(start, end), val = val)))

Dennis

